 "notes": "Headline curve: 90% C.L. (CLs) upper bound on the ALP dark-matter axioelectric coupling g_ae vs ALP mass (0.8-500 keV), Fig. 5 left, thick solid red EDELWEISS-III line, digitised from the e-print raster figure alp_dm.png via color/connected-component tracing (axis calibration from decade ticks; verified curve start at 0.8 keV and overlay agreement). Assumes local DM density 0.3 GeV/cm^3 and <v>=1e-3 c (Eq. 3). The paper also reports a solar-axion CBRD bound g_ae<1.1e-11 (Fig. 3) and a 14.4 keV solar bound g_ae*g_aN_eff<3.5e-17 (Fig. 4), plus a hidden-photon kinetic-mixing bound (Fig. 5 right); the ALP-DM g_ae curve is reported here as the main mass-dependent electron-coupling result. Curve downsampled to 110 points by Douglas-Peucker in log-log space (max interpolation deviation 12%). Dashed 'EDELWEISS upgrade' lines in Fig. 5 are projections and excluded.",
